00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:29,333
There are those who sweep and those who pay others to sweep.

2
00:10:46,666 --> 00:10:52,666
The Door is a drama film directed by István Szabó.

3
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Emerenc, an elderly and private woman, is hired to be the
housekeeper of a struggling writer, Magda.

4
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:39,333
An event in the writer's life prompts Emerenc to disclose details of her
traumatizing past, which will bond the two women forever.

5
00:26:56,666 --> 00:27:02,666
Based on the novel by Magda Szabó.

6
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Emerenc Szeredás, played by Helen Mirren.

7
00:37:43,333 --> 00:37:49,333
Magda, played by Martina Gedeck.

8
00:43:06,666 --> 00:43:12,666
Tibor, played by Károly Eperjes.

9
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:36,000
Mr. Brodarics, played by Péter Andorai.

10
00:53:53,333 --> 00:53:59,333
Sutu, played by Enikő Börcsök.

11
00:59:16,666 --> 00:59:22,666
The Lt. Colonel, played by Gábor Koncz.

12
01:04:40,000 --> 01:04:46,000
The Door (Hungarian: Az ajtó) is a 2012 English-language Hungarian drama film
directed by István Szabó and starring Martina Gedeck and Helen Mirren.

13
01:10:03,333 --> 01:10:09,333
It is based on the Hungarian novel of the same name concerning the relationship of a
novelist (Gedeck) and her eccentric maid (Mirren) in early-1970s Hungary.

14
01:15:26,666 --> 01:15:32,666
The film was selected to be featured in the competition programme
at the 34th Moscow International Film Festival.

15
01:20:50,000 --> 01:20:56,000
It also won the Michael Curtiz Audience Award at the Hungarian
Film Festival of Los Angeles in November 2012.

16
01:26:13,333 --> 01:26:19,333
The film explores themes of budapest, hungary,
cat, married couple, author, maid.

17
01:31:36,666 --> 01:31:42,666
The tone is emotional.
